{
  "_readme": [
    "Where wild flowers generate, how often, in which Botania colors, and with how many Flower Patch blocks.",
    "Applied at world load by kubejs/server_scripts/worldgen/wild_flowers.js (CEConfig [worldgen.systems] wildFlowers).",
    "Rejoin the world after editing; only chunks generated afterwards change. Reference + tests: feature_writeup/flowers.md.",
    "Resolved numbers per biome, gaps and color coverage: feature_writeup/flowers_by_biome.md (python3 tools/gen_wild_flowers.py).",
    "",
    "Biomes and traits: the 'biomes' table in wild_crops.json (one table for both systems; add a new mod's biomes there).",
    "Biomes marked ocean or cave never get flowers from this file.",
    "",
    "Rates are flower patches per chunk: '1/8' = one patch per 8 chunks, '2' = two per chunk. A rate becomes a placement",
    "tier (c<N> = N per chunk, r<N> = one in N chunks), so close rates round to the same tier.",
    "A selector is a biome id (has ':') or a trait clause ('cold grassy !snowy': all must hold, '!x' must not).",
    "rates: [[selector, rate], ...] per-biome overrides of 'rate', first match wins.",
    "",
    "density: multiplies every rate this file adds (botania and flowers; not 'existing').",
    "heightmap: where pack patches are centred. MOTION_BLOCKING_NO_LEAVES puts them on forest floors, not tree tops.",
    "tall_flowers: blocks two high; an entry with one is a random_patch (bone meal never grows it) instead of a flower patch.",
    "",
    "flower_patch: Flower Patch blocks (2-4 flowers in one block) mixed into wild flowers.",
    "  share: fraction of the small flowers in pack patches ('flowers') that are Flower Patch blocks. Per entry: flower_patch.",
    "  existing_share: the same for the biome files' flower features ('existing'). Per feature: existing.<id>.flower_patch.",
    "  sizes: relative weights of 2, 3 and 4-flower patches.",
    "  blocks: flower -> its patch block ({\"block\": id, \"property\": name} when the count property isn't 'flowers').",
    "  Dual-noise providers (the meadow's) can't take patch blocks; the meadow gets them from the 'meadow' entry.",
    "",
    "botania: Botania's mystical flowers. Its own modifier is switched off (disable_modifiers).",
    "  palettes: biome -> the colors that grow there, space separated; 'color*N' = N times as likely. '_default' covers",
    "  biomes not listed; an empty palette = no Botania flowers. Each patch is one color picked from the palette.",
    "  rate / rates / density as above. Keep every one of the 16 colors in some common biome: petals are crafting inputs.",
    "",
    "flowers: patches the pack adds.",
    "  blocks: {block: weight}; where / add / except: as wild_crops.json; rate / rates / density; patch: {tries, xz_spread,",
    "  y_spread} (default 48 / 6 / 3); flower_patch: share override; disable_modifiers: mod modifiers this replaces.",
    "",
    "existing: flower features the biome files list (Terralith ships the overworld's). Keys are placed feature ids from",
    "  flower_features.json (generated snapshot). scale: rate multiplier, 0 = removed everywhere; remove: selectors of",
    "  biomes it is taken out of; flower_patch: share override. Unlisted features keep their rate."
  ],

  "density": 1,
  "heightmap": "MOTION_BLOCKING_NO_LEAVES",
  "tall_flowers": ["minecraft:sunflower", "minecraft:lilac", "minecraft:rose_bush", "minecraft:peony"],

  "flower_patch": {
    "share": 0.25,
    "existing_share": 0.15,
    "sizes": {"2": 3, "3": 2, "4": 1},
    "blocks": {
      "minecraft:allium": "flowerpatch:allium_patch",
      "minecraft:azure_bluet": "flowerpatch:azure_bluet_patch",
      "minecraft:blue_orchid": "flowerpatch:blue_orchid_patch",
      "minecraft:cornflower": "flowerpatch:cornflower_patch",
      "minecraft:dandelion": "flowerpatch:dandelion_patch",
      "minecraft:lily_of_the_valley": "flowerpatch:lily_of_the_valley_patch",
      "minecraft:orange_tulip": "flowerpatch:orange_tulip_patch",
      "minecraft:oxeye_daisy": "flowerpatch:oxeye_daisy_patch",
